coder › Implemented `match(pattern, path)` in `src/router.ts` and added tests in `src/router.test.ts` on branch `feat/router-match` (2 commits).

What changed:
- `src/router.ts`: `match` splits pattern/path on `/` after trimming leading/trailing slashes (so trailing slash on either side is ignored), strips the `?query` part of `path`, compares segment counts, maps `:name` segments to one non-empty path segment each, maps a final `*` to one-or-more remaining segments joined with `/` as `rest` (no match when nothing follows), percent-decodes params via `decodeURIComponent`, and throws `TypeError` when `*` appears in any non-final pattern segment.
- `src/router.test.ts`: 9 tests covering static match, named params, non-matches, trailing slashes, query strings, percent-decoding, wildcard single/multi-segment, wildcard-with-nothing-after (no match), and `TypeError` for non-final `*`.

Decisions not in the plan:
- Static segments are compared raw (not percent-decoded); only captured params are decoded.
- An undecodable (`%`-invalid) captured segment is treated as no-match (`undefined`) rather than throwing.
- `*`-only and root patterns fall out of the same logic (e.g. `*` matches any non-empty path as `rest`).

